      "evidenceStrength": "**Weakest topic, and largely mechanistic.** Choosing exercises \"by resistance profile\" makes sense biomechanically (based on the long-muscle-length research), but direct trials are few and mixed. Larsen 2025 found dumbbell and cable lateral raises grew the deltoid about equally, despite their different resistance curves. Schwanbeck 2020 found free weights and machines gave similar growth. The regional-growth claim rests on Kassiano 2022, a systematic review of 8 small studies in young men, so treat it as suggestive. The claim that stability helps growth is mostly a logical inference (less balance limitation lets you get closer to failure); no verified direct hypertrophy trial on it was found.",
